  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- BREAKING: every runtime command now requires a valid octoevidence.json with a non-empty knowledgeRoot. There is no fallback to the source repository; init scaffolds knowledge_base for a local project.\n- Uniform knowledge layout: every bundle lives directly at <knowledgeRoot>/<area>/<name>, including brd/<slug> and trd/<slug>. Unit names and bundle paths are identical; there is no okf marker.\n- Module access: modules map contained source folders to exact units or area wildcards. readwrite is ownership; read is visibility only. Missing, external, or link-escaping source folders are rejected.\n- Ownership-safe synchronization: read-only drift is visible but never gates, and pull applies only to explicitly owned remote-only or remote-ahead units. MCP mutation metadata reflects that an approved pull may overwrite or delete bundle documents.\n- Agent guidance now treats OKF as a compact, cited map for targeted understanding while keeping checked-out source code and active configuration authoritative for current implementation mechanics and state.\n- Deterministic BRD/TRD workflows include DOCX extraction, typed registers, coverage and blocking analysis, platform views, test coverage, Git history, reverse relations, and requirement-to-code traceability.\n- CLI, MCP, generated agent assets, package smoke tests, README, product contract, and architecture documentation describe the same configuration and layout.",
